# 💻 Practice 2 — Creating Number Pairs

```python
numbers = [1, 2, 3]

result = [(x, y) for x in numbers for y in numbers]

print(result)
```

### Output

```text
[(1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 3),
 (2, 1), (2, 2), (2, 3),
 (3, 1), (3, 2), (3, 3)]
```

---

# 💻 Practice 3 — Flattening a Nested List

```python
numbers = [[1, 2], [3, 4], [5, 6]]

result = [number for inner_list in numbers for number in inner_list]

print(result)
```

### Output

```text
[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
```

### Logic

```text
Nested List
    ↓
Take inner list
    ↓
Take each value from inner list
    ↓
Store in a new list
```

